rduous process  of applying  for a new work permit 16 bc firefighters  who tested positive for kova 19  are under quarantine tonight after  returning home from the front lines  in california the bc wildfire service  says three initial cases were reported  in the u.s  13 more were confirmed after crews  returned home  it's unclear how the first three were  infected but contact tracing  is now underway 223 bc firefighters were  sent to california to help with the  state's  worst wildfire season on record  more than 7.5 million people in  california alone  have voted early in the u.s presidential  election  they're among the record 75 million  americans  who've already cast ballots nationwide  voters are keen to get the results but  every state has its own rules when it  comes to processing and counting  mail-in ballots jackson proskow reports  on the looming chaos  in the final count in pennsylvania  they've already received  2 million mail-in ballots the monumental  task of opening and counting them can't  begin  until election day we have to be patient  people have to know the system is  different in different  states the three states that decided the  last election  will be the last to start counting their  mail-in ballots  the result may be no result for days  wisconsin says it won't count all its  ballots until november 4th  michigan and pennsylvania say it could  take until friday november 6 to declare  a winner  there are some states where you might  see president trump winning  on election night or early on election  night but once these mail-in ballots are  counted  even the next day or a day later that  they could switch  the potential confusion cuts both ways  the in-place states that could decide  the presidency quickly  do allow for an early count arizona  florida and north carolina will deliver  the bulk of mail-in and in-person  results on election night  it would be very very proper and very  nice if  a winner were declared on november 3rd  there are fears trump may seek to  exploit delays that are already  built into the system even though states  have weeks to certify their results  you may have president trump declare  victory on the first day if he is ahead  in some states and then he may then say  that it's fraudulent  as the absentee ballots are counted  there are also fears of potential court  challenges targeting the results  a decisive win by either candidate makes  that less likely  the bigger worry may be all the ballots  that are still outstanding  states are waiting on millions of them  to be returned amidst new warnings about  heavy delays with the u.s postal system  americans are now being urged to drop  off their ballots in person  to add a little certainty to this  uncertain election  robin jackson frosco in washington  thanks jackson  kova 19 is a major issue in the final  stretch of the campaign  and both candidates have very different  approaches to the health crisis  as mike armstrong reports from west  virginia there's a huge difference  between  how their supporters see it too  this state is about as red as they get  the latest poll in west virginia gives  donald trump a two to one advantage  it's not that there aren't many biden  signs here there aren't even many trump  signs the campaign doesn't need them  i feel confident yeah gail hartley is  doing her part with the trump flag  and jokes that west virginians sort of  get ignored during presidential  elections  i think the last presidential candidate  we had was george bush  that's a while ago that's a while ago we  don't we don't see them  now what this state has in common with  others is its  struggle with covet 19. the seven day  average of positive tests has jumped  close to 50 percent over the last three  weeks  there's a severe upswing west virginia  has 10 days of early voting at one point  they had to close a polling station  after a polling worker tested positive  despite that when the president  complains about  coverage of cov